import Lean

/-
The simp sets of the step tactics (NoCompiler/Tactic.lean). They are applied in
separate passes on purpose: one `simp` call that both unfolds the semantics
and reduces literal arithmetic produces a single definitional step the kernel
can only check by unfolding `+` on a symbolic operand, which recurses through
a 64-bit literal one successor at a time. Separate passes keep each
definitional step small.
-/

/-- Pass 1: unfold the semantics of one instruction. -/
register_simp_attr nocompiler_sem
/-- Pass 2: state projections and register reads. -/
register_simp_attr nocompiler_state
/-- Pass 3: arithmetic on literals. -/
register_simp_attr nocompiler_lit
/-- The instruction at each address of a code image, one `rfl` lemma per
    address, generated by `nocompiler export`. Used with pass 2. -/
register_simp_attr nocompiler_image
/-- The word normal form of NoCompiler/Auto.lean: every word as `BitVec.ofNat 64 e`
    or `base + BitVec.ofNat 64 e` for a natural-number expression `e`, and
    comparisons and memory accesses on such words as facts about `e`. -/
register_simp_attr nocompiler_nat
